SHASTRATH - Sacred Scripture Arena (Dharma Yuddha)
=================================================

A scripture quiz battle arena. Answer riddles from the Mahabharata, Ramayana,
Vedas and Puranas, and strike down your rival before they strike you.

PLAY LOCALLY
------------
1. pip install aiohttp
2. python server.py   (the game opens automatically)

The server serves the game AND the backend from the same address, so the game
connects to the server it was loaded from - no waiting, no cold start.

PLAY ONLINE FROM ANYWHERE
-------------------------
- Permanent: deploy this folder to Render / Railway / Fly.io
  (start command: python server.py). Render reads render.yaml.
  Those hosts set PORT themselves; share the https URL they give you.
- The Android app (APK) loads the game straight from https://shastrarth.onrender.com
  so it always uses the hosted backend. After every change to the backend you
  must push to GitHub so Render redeploys.
- Same Wi-Fi: use the "Same Wi-Fi" address printed in the console.
  Set NO_TUNNEL=1 to disable the automatic cloudflared tunnel.

GAME MODES
----------
- 1P Solo (vs Bot) / 2P Duel / 3P Tri-Yuddha / 4P Kurukshetra
- Battle length: 6, 12, 18, 24 or 40 rounds
- Realms: Mahabharata, Ramayana, Vedas, Puranas or All Scriptures
- Difficulty: I Easy, II Harder, III Scholar, or Rising (auto ramp)
- Masters of Shastrath (Hardcore): Scholar (level 3) riddles only,
  lethal 50 HP, sharper Asura, 3x Karma
- Online play: share the room code or the invite link. Same room +
  same settings = same arena.

A question never repeats inside the same match, and every rematch draws
fresh ("unseen") riddles.

ADDING QUESTIONS
----------------
- Open www/questions.json and copy any entry.
  epic:   M = Mahabharata, R = Ramayana, V = Vedas, P = Puranas
  level:  1 = Easy, 2 = Harder, 3 = Scholar
  options: exactly 4   |   answer: 0-3 (position of the correct option)
- The game shuffles the options itself, so the answer index stays valid.
- Keep questions.json next to server.py OR inside www/ (both are detected).
- No server restart needed - the file is re-read automatically.
- OPTIONAL TRANSLATION:
  "tr": {"hi": {"q": "...", "options": [4 items in the SAME order as English]}}
  codes: hi, mr, sa, ta, te. Missing languages fall back to English.

ANDROID APK
-----------
1. npx cap copy android      (copies www/ into the app)
2. Build the APK:
   - Android Studio: open the android/ folder -> Build -> Build APK(s)
     (the APK lands in android/app/build/outputs/apk/release/), or
   - command line:  cd android && gradlew assembleRelease
   The result is copied to release/SHASTRATH-release-unsigned.apk
3. SIGN IT (Android Studio: Build -> Generate Signed App Bundle/APK, or):
   sign-apk.bat  path\to\key.jks  alias  storePassword  keyPassword
   -> writes SHASTRATH-release.apk to your Downloads folder.
   (To sign automatically with Gradle, drop the keystore next to the project
   as android/keystore.properties with storeFile / storePassword / keyAlias /
   keyPassword, then run gradlew assembleRelease again.)

IMPORTANT - the app loads the game from https://shastrarth.onrender.com
(capacitor.config.json -> server.url), so after every backend change you must
push to GitHub so Render redeploys. The APK then picks up the new game with no
rebuild. To bundle the game inside the APK instead, delete the "server" block
from capacitor.config.json and run npx cap copy android again.

Set the app name / id in capacitor.config.json (appName: SHASTRATH).
The app id is com.dharmyudha.app - keep it the same to update an existing
install, or change it to install alongside the old one.

FILES
-----
- server.py            backend: match engine, question bank, websocket
- www/index.html       the game (single page app)
- www/style.css        themes + animations
- www/lang.js          all on-screen text (6 languages)
- www/questions.json   the question bank
- www/bg.jpg           background art
- android/             Capacitor Android project
